That's right, with each day that passes, people continue about their lives as before, showing no signs of stopping or slowing down, much like the relentless waves crashing forward in an ocean. This only serves to reaffirm their determination rather than indicating any wavering of it. It seems as though the cycle will repeat until this point is reached again, demonstrating the cyclical nature of actions and reactions in a self-perpetuating loop. Is there anything more fitting under these circumstances than to acknowledge the occurrence of another milestone, signaling yet another round of efforts and achievements? It feels as though we're observing history being made, one step at a time.

This observation doesn't change the objective reality; it merely confirms it. As time marches on, indifference and action become one and the same, reinforcing each other in a virtuous cycle. The only plausible explanation is that we're witnessing the start of a new series of events, once again. 

It's clear that we haven't seen the end;
